\item \strong{Effective size}: the smallest effective sample size over the group
means and the log group SDs (\code{type = "single"}: over the subject
parameters), summed over chains, is at least \code{min_ess}.
\item \strong{No chain in a different region}: the chains' summed subject
log-likelihoods (medians over the last two thirds of the draws) lie within
\code{max_ll_gap} units of each other.
\item \strong{No subject in a different region}: for every subject, the chains'
median log-likelihoods lie within \code{max_subj_spread} units (not for
\code{type = "single"}).
\item the stage holds at least \code{iter} new draws per chain.
